---
// The typography guide, shown under "Typography Builder" in the Builder
// Guide (src/pages/website-builder/index.astro).
---

<p>
  Set site-wide styles for headings, paragraphs, emphasis, strong text, code,
  citations, preformatted text, and block quotations. Then give each theme group
  area (page, hero, and sections) its own typography. It travels with the theme
  group's classes, so assigning a theme group in the Page Builder applies its
  colors and typography together.
</p>
<p>
  Blank fields keep existing site styles, or follow site-wide defaults when
  editing a section. Changes stay in the preview until you save the stylesheet.
  Saved rules override Tailwind typography utilities. Inline styles, important
  declarations, and more-specific unlayered CSS can still take priority.
</p>
<p>
  In Chrome or Edge on localhost or HTTPS, click Save to project. The first
  time, choose the websitebuilder project folder; it is remembered after that,
  shared with the Theme Builder. Site-wide defaults are saved to the typography
  section of <code>src/styles/themes/sitewide.css</code>, next to the sitewide
  colors from the Theme Builder; theme group typography is saved with the theme
  group and written to <code>src/styles/themes/groups.css</code>. If folder
  access fails, use Save directly to CSS for the defaults, then Rewrite
  groups.css &amp; theme-groups.json in the Theme Builder.
</p>
